  "chunk": "to the mailbox and attempts to open it, only to find it empty. This does\nnot suggest an intelligent form of thinking; any human player would remember\nthat the mailbox was already opened. ChatGPT showed this kind of repetitive\nbehaviour in multiple situations during the game. This also explains the large\nnumber of moves (due to repeated actions) whilst limited progress was made in\nthe game, as discussed in Section 4.\nMoreover, it seems that none of the chatbots learn from their previous runs\neven though they have access to the chat and conversation history. That is,\nmistakes made during one iteration are often repeated later in the same itera-\ntion or in following iterations, suggesting a lack of metacognition — the ability\nto monitor and reflect on one’s own thinking processes [10, 27]. Although no\nhuman players were included in the experimental setup, one would assume that\na human player of any skill level would not repeatedly reconsider actions that",
